    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39589" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">punctus</span></b> , ūs (form punctus,
		i, <i><span class="en">Isid. Orig. 3, 121</span></i>), m.
		pungo. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A pricking</i>, <i>stinging; a
			prick</i>, <i>sting</i>, <i>puncture</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oculis punctu erutis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					29, 6, 38, § 131</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">App. M. 7, p. 196, 11</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Scrib. Comp. 206, 208, 209</span></i>.
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A point</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mundi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					2, 68, 68, § 174</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Isid. Orig. 11, 1</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
